       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** You may have meant a different number.\n\nIf you want a different dose, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy before it's entered."
